{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"The lower-level win maps now give a concrete dense metric: along a terminal’s axis, the projected logical cells form an unbroken chain. Level 1 accepts every row but exactly one column; level 2’s four winning tuples are precisely the configurations whose projected columns fill every 4-pixel step between the ports. For level 6, the first low-cost states satisfying both projected-axis chains are only 38 candidates, so I’m testing that bounded set before broadening the topology."}}
