{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"The corrected elbow map supplies the missing directional rule: in the known level-5 win, the elbow must sit on the socket’s row, left of its feeder, while the feeder must be below it. Applied to level 6, the two L-shapes can turn the top-down source at the right-socket row; a vertical bar placed to their left can fan that leftward branch to both left-socket rows. I’m testing that specific turn–carrier topology with the marked horizontal bar kept on the source/bottom-target column."}}
